{"name":"Yellow Magic Orchestra","hex":"#dcc449","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"},{"term":"magic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The application of rituals or actions, especially those based on occult knowledge, to subdue or manipulate natural or supernatural beings and forces in order to have some benefit from them. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The supernatural forces which are drawn on in such a ritual."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having supernatural talents, properties or qualities attributed to magic.","Producing extraordinary results, as though through the use of magic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magic"},{"term":"orchestra","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large group of musicians who play together on various instruments, usually including some from strings, woodwind, brass and/or percussion; the instruments played by such a group.","A semicircular space in front of the stage used by the chorus in Ancient Greek and Hellenistic theatres."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orchestra"}],"entries":[{"title":"Yellow Magic Orchestra","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow Magic Orchestra was a Japanese electronic music band formed in Tokyo in 1978 by Haruomi Hosono, Yukihiro Takahashi and Ryuichi Sakamoto. The group is considered influential and innovative in the field of popular electronic music. They were pioneers in their use of synthesizers, samplers, sequencers, drum machines, computers, and digital recording technology, and effectively anticipated the \"electropop boom\" of the 1980s. They are credited with playing a key role in the development of several electronic genres, including synthpop, J-pop, electro, and techno, while exploring subversive sociopolitical themes throughout their career."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Yellow_Magic_Orchestra_YMO_%281981_Press_Photo%29.jpg/330px-Yellow_Magic_Orchestra_YMO_%281981_Press_Photo%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow_Magic_Orchestra","wikidata":"Q854590"},{"title":"Yellow Magic Orchestra (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow Magic Orchestra is the debut studio album by Japanese electronic music band Yellow Magic Orchestra. Originally released by Alfa Records, in Japan in 1978, the album was released by A&M Records in Europe and the United States and Canada in early 1979, with the US version featuring new cover art but without the closing track of \"Acrobat\". Both versions would later be re-issued in 2003 as a double-disc format, with the American version as the first disc."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/37/YMO_YelloyMagicOrchestra.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow_Magic_Orchestra_(album)","wikidata":"Q8051764"},{"title":"Orchestra","blocks":[{"text":"An orchestra is a large instrumental ensemble typical of classical music or jazz, which combines instruments from different families. There are typically four main sections of instruments:"},{"items":["The string section, including the violin, viola, cello, and double bass","The woodwind section, including the flute, oboe, clarinet, and bassoon, and sometimes piccolo, cor anglais, bass clarinet, contrabassoon, and saxophone","The brass section, including the French horn, trumpet, trombone, and tuba, and sometimes cornet and euphonium","The percussion section, including the timpani, snare drum, bass drum, cymbals, triangle, tambourine, tam-tam and mallet percussion instruments"]}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/National_Chamber_Orchestra_of_Armenia.jpg/330px-National_Chamber_Orchestra_of_Armenia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orchestra","wikidata":"Q42998"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow","wikidata":"Q943"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Roland_TR-808_drum_machine.jpg/330px-Roland_TR-808_drum_machine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Roland_TR-808_drum_machine.jpg/330px-Roland_TR-808_drum_machine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"YMO were the first band to use the Roland TR-808 Rhythm Composer, which has appeared on more hit records than any other drum machine.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoland_TR-808_drum_machine.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Cincinnati_Symphony_Orchestra_Wikivoyage_FTT.jpg/500px-Cincinnati_Symphony_Orchestra_Wikivoyage_FTT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Cincinnati_Symphony_Orchestra_Wikivoyage_FTT.jpg/1280px-Cincinnati_Symphony_Orchestra_Wikivoyage_FTT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Cincinnati_Symphony_Orchestra_Wikivoyage_FTT.jpg/500px-Cincinnati_Symphony_Orchestra_Wikivoyage_FTT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cincinnati Symphony Orchestra","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACincinnati_Symphony_Orchestra_Wikivoyage_FTT.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Philadelphia_Orchestra_at_American_premiere_of_Mahler%27s_8th_Symphony_%281916%29.jpg/500px-Philadelphia_Orchestra_at_American_premiere_of_Mahler%27s_8th_Symphony_%281916%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Philadelphia_Orchestra_at_American_premiere_of_Mahler%27s_8th_Symphony_%281916%29.jpg/1280px-Philadelphia_Orchestra_at_American_premiere_of_Mahler%27s_8th_Symphony_%281916%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Philadelphia_Orchestra_at_American_premiere_of_Mahler%27s_8th_Symphony_%281916%29.jpg/500px-Philadelphia_Orchestra_at_American_premiere_of_Mahler%27s_8th_Symphony_%281916%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stokowski and the Philadelphia Orchestra at the 2 March 1916 American premiere of Mahler's 8th Symphony","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhiladelphia_Orchestra_at_American_premiere_of_Mahler's_8th_Symphony_(1916).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Gruppenfoto_BJO_Winter_2012.jpeg/500px-Gruppenfoto_BJO_Winter_2012.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Gruppenfoto_BJO_Winter_2012.jpeg/1280px-Gruppenfoto_BJO_Winter_2012.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Gruppenfoto_BJO_Winter_2012.jpeg/500px-Gruppenfoto_BJO_Winter_2012.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Group photo of Bundesjugendorchester, 2012","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGruppenfoto_BJO_Winter_2012.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Orchestre_symphonique_%28dessus%29.jpg/500px-Orchestre_symphonique_%28dessus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Orchestre_symphonique_%28dessus%29.jpg/1280px-Orchestre_symphonique_%28dessus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Orchestre_symphonique_%28dessus%29.jpg/500px-Orchestre_symphonique_%28dessus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Symphonic orchestra, on stage, seen from above","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOrchestre_symphonique_(dessus).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/49/Laredo_Philharmonic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=th